                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ebd8aabe-fbc9-3e92-87f4-d7bca790eb0d",
                        "entry_id": "fcaa52a1-6b01-3efc-88b2-fd9ca67a2763",
                        "glosses": [
                            "An orthomorphic map projection, in which meridians appear at right-angles to the equator, and lines of latitude are horizontal lines whose distance from each other increases with distance from the equator."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "attributive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "1d6cb6aa-3a48-4171-96d4-96015a0b352c",
                                "sense_id": "ebd8aabe-fbc9-3e92-87f4-d7bca790eb0d",
                                "text": "we have determined to go by way of Lisbon […] , if so be that Capt. Kidd our gallant or rather gallows commander understands plain sailing and Mercator, and takes us on our voyage all according to the Chart."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1d88c19e-9c6e-4350-aac0-07b0e06bc786",
                                "sense_id": "ebd8aabe-fbc9-3e92-87f4-d7bca790eb0d",
                                "text": "The Mercator has been a favorite schoolroom map because it shows almost the whole world simply—in a single continuous panel. It does not seem to distort shapes."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3f4ac100-6aea-461e-8a9d-c4db3ed59ed1",
                                "sense_id": "ebd8aabe-fbc9-3e92-87f4-d7bca790eb0d",
                                "text": "In the Mercator projection, the line of intersection between the cylinder and the sphere is the equator, while in the Traverse Mercator this line is a meridian."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "278ac33c-cc58-491b-8320-6348b2f66e1c",
                                "sense_id": "ebd8aabe-fbc9-3e92-87f4-d7bca790eb0d",
                                "text": "Most digital maps are displayed in the Web Mercator projection but this is slowly changing. Web Mercator became the default standard for web mapping when the major online map services adopted it, like Google and OpenStreetMap."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d664ddd3-27d8-42bd-ae5e-450ad78890e5",
                                "sense_id": "ebd8aabe-fbc9-3e92-87f4-d7bca790eb0d",
                                "text": "[…] saying the Mercator fostered a false impression that Africa was “marginal”, despite being the world’s second-largest continent by area, with more than 1 billion people."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
